Z||000000||Shaun41178||09-21-1999||09:27 AM||||Well I ordered a Gm cam a while back and all the matching hardware to go with the cam.  I had no idea that the cam did not come with lifters.  The cam is part number 12363220. which is the one with .427 lift intake and .454 lift exhaust and is the one that is used in the 3.4 engine.  So how much were lifters for this cam people?<P>So anyway I get quoted $99 for the cam and then $100 for all the matching hardware for the cam with a special discount price from someone who my dad knows that works at a GM dealership.  So thats a total of $200 roughly correct?  Well the guy called today and quoted me that the total is now $449 with the special discount price.  I said WHAT!!!  Now come on people.  I know some out there have bought all this same stuff so I want to know how much this all cost you.<P>Basically I told the guy to get me the cam with the matching springs, retainers, pushrods, keepers.  First I was quoted $200 now he wants $449.  It would seem to me that the $449 is before the discounted price but I guess I need to go talk to the guy to make sure.  Help me out people.  How much did you guys pay for this stuff.  Thanks   <P>Shaun &lt;---- getting ripped off??<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Eric||09-21-1999||04:09 PM||||Can you still take the stuff back?  Sounds like you got screwed.  When I ordered that very same cam it cost me $114.52 (no discount)and came with lifters, but it was the "cam kit" (12364059) not the (12363220) performance 3.4 camshaft.  I didn't order any other part of the valvetrain because my machinist is going to build it up from small chevy parts.  The place I got it from was Boman's Chevrolet in Hebron, Ohio.  It would be too far to drive from Toledo, but they should be able to tell you where to get your parts from in your area.  The phone # is <BR>1-800-948-7277.  They are right down the street from National Trails Raceway so they deal with a lot of performance parts.||||reg||13
Z||000002||Patrick||09-21-1999||04:20 PM||||<BR>Part of the problem might be that you're buying from a GM dealership. That's usually the LAST place you'd want to purchase anything from unless you want to pay extra. And I don't think that you or anyone else wants to do that...<P>||||reg||13
Z||000003||GREENDANO||09-21-1999||05:26 PM||||I know my cam came with lifters and was much less than $400 with all the extras.  But, I work at a dealership, so I pay 10% over cost.  Still, That sounds like too much money.  I know someone in the past has mentioned about a dealership that is Fiero sympathetic and gives a good discount to Fiero People. Plus, I hear they will even ship the parts to you.  That's a bonus for sure.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||4
Z||000004||Shaun41178||09-22-1999||04:51 PM||||UPDATE!!!<P>Well I went and talked to the guy at the Dealership who is giving me everything wholesale.  Well the cam that I ordered did not come with lifters but it was priced at what he said which was $99.  Everything else was priced correctly too except for get this, $98 for 12 pushrods.  Thats $8.18 a piece for a pushrod.  So I said to send those back cause I am not paying $98 for pushrods.  Doesn't Crane or TRW make pushrods for like $20-$30?  Also since the cam did not come with lifters I had to order the lifters for the cam.  How much you ask for 12 lifters?, $130!!!!  So I said no way.  Send those back.<P>So after some discussion I ordered the Cam kit which was $117 or so and that came with the lifters and has the exact same lift and duration as the otehr cam I was going to get.  So instead of paying $239 for a cam and lifters I am paying $117.  <P>So I had him send the original cam back along with the lifters and pushrods.  So now this should bring everything back down to the price of what I was ecpecting which was about $200 or so.<P>The cam kit was part number 12364059.  It states right in the performance book that this cam is not legal on pollution controlled vehicles.  I am not worried about that as much as the lobe centerline of 112 degrees as opposed to 107 from the other cam I was going to get.  Anyone know if this will effect the computer at all?  I sure hope it doesn't or I am going to be pissed.  Thanks||||reg||14
